# XCU tput
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The sequences are terminal dependent and the page leaves the results
# undefined when standard output is not a terminal, so nothing observable is
# left for a script. The exit codes for a usage error and an unknown terminal
# are not exercised, since the page gives no result for a non-terminal output.

assertion  XCU.tput.001
anchor     utilities/tput.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/tput.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/tput.html#EXIT STATUS
class      untestable
says       tput clear, init and reset write the terminal's clear, initialise and
           reset sequences, a terminal that lacks one is not an error, and the
           exit status classes name usage errors, unknown terminals and invalid
           operands.
reason     The sequences depend on the terminal type, and the page leaves the
           results undefined when standard output is not a terminal.
